        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> 42, 5⁴</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 42, 5⁴</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H verdeutlicht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H makes this explicit</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Zwischensatz gilt auch für die folgenden in Unzucht (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 9) ertappten Frauen und bezeichnet handhafte Tat im Ggs. zu nachträglicher Klage auf Ehebruch (<hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 10) od. Unzucht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The parenthetical clause applies also to the women caught in unchastity (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 9) who follow, and denotes an offence caught in the act, in contrast to a subsequent charge of adultery (<hi rend="italic">above</hi> 10) or unchastity</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘eingeschlossen durch Türen’ H cor., Af’s Dat. absol. nicht verstehend</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘shut in by doors’ H cor., not understanding Af’s dat. absol.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">coopertura</hi> Hn besser als Q</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">coopertura</hi> Hn better than Q</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Familie 6; Bastard 7a. b; Eheschliessung 1. b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Familie 6; Bastard 7a. b; Eheschliessung 1. b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Schwester und Mutter stehen zwar, solange der Hausvater lebt, unter dessen Munt. Doch sagt Af nicht, dass erst nach jenes Tode das Fehderecht auf jeden Sohn übergehe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sister and mother are indeed under the mund of the head of the household as long as he lives. But Af does not say that the right of feud passes to each son only after his death</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-7.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[setze diese Zahl zu ‘oder’] Die Lesung in E, ohne <hi rend="italic">æwum,</hi> heisst ‘angeboren’, was unnütz wäre; doch steht dies auch neben <hi rend="italic">mæg</hi> 42, 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">[put this number at ‘oder’] The reading in E, without <hi rend="italic">æwum,</hi> means ‘inborn’, which would be pointless; yet this also stands beside <hi rend="italic">mæg</hi> 42, 6</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-7.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>æt</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid</hi>. H.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 18 is printed 4 times on the page (42.7, 42.7, 42.7, 42.7), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-7.attnote.fn.18-2" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>æt</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid</hi>. H.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 18 is printed 4 times on the page (42.7, 42.7, 42.7, 42.7), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-7.attnote.fn.18-3" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>æt</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid</hi>. H.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 18 is printed 4 times on the page (42.7, 42.7, 42.7, 42.7), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-7.attnote.fn.18-4" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>æt</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid</hi>. H.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 18 is printed 4 times on the page (42.7, 42.7, 42.7, 42.7), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-7.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>betynedum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">betynede</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-7.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>æwum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">H.</seg></note>
